# PREIshare — agent rules

Grounded in `docs/onboarding/`. Do not invent paths, scripts, or folders that are not in `docs/onboarding/repo-map.md`.

## Project identity

PREIshare is a real-estate intelligence product. This checkout is a **single-package npm app** at the repo root (`src/`), not a monorepo. Prefer existing patterns over greenfield frameworks.

## Stack (do not substitute)

- Language: TypeScript (strict `tsconfig.json`)
- App: TanStack Start + React, Vite (`vite.config.ts`), file routes in `src/routes/`, UI in `src/components/`, styles in `src/styles.css`, router in `src/router.tsx`
- Package manager: npm + `package-lock.json` (do not treat a leftover `"pnpm"` block as a decision)
- Backend/data (intended; **not in this tree yet**): Supabase, PostgreSQL, pgvector — no `supabase/` folder, no `@supabase` dependency, no `src/lib/supabase.ts`
- Collaboration: Git + GitHub pull requests (fork → feature branch → PR; do not push to the team repo)

## Where to work (new contributors)

- Read first: `docs/onboarding/repo-map.md`, `docs/onboarding/team-orientation-notes.md`, `README.md`
- Safe first-touch: `docs/onboarding/` (orientation, setup-log, repo-map). Tiny `README.md` copy only if a mentor agrees. No `CONTRIBUTORS` file in this clone.
- `src/lib/user.ts` is a UI stub (`getUser()` returns `null`), not a database client.
- Avoid unless explicitly tasked: `src/routes/`, `src/components/`, `src/router.tsx`, `vite.config.ts`, `src/routeTree.gen.ts` (generated — never hand-edit), `package.json` / `package-lock.json` deps, inventing `.github/` CI, auth, payments, migrations, vector/search core

## How to change code

- Never delete, `git rm`, or empty tracked files unless the user explicitly names those paths and says to delete them. Do not slim a PR by removing onboarding docs or other existing work from the branch.
- Prefer the smallest diff that completes the requested task
- Match neighboring naming, file layout, and TypeScript style (`src/components/` Header, Footer, ThemeToggle)
- Do not drive-by refactor, add libraries, or add lint/format/test tooling the repo-map says is absent
- Do not invent `src/lib/supabase.ts`, a `test` script, or other paths/scripts not listed in the repo-map

## Secrets and safety

- Never commit `.env`, API keys, tokens, or connection strings (`.env` is gitignored; there is no `.env.example`)
- Never paste secrets into docs, rules, chat, or the setup-log
- Do not invent credentials or touch production databases (none are wired in this checkout)
- If a change needs configuration, document the variable **name** only, never a real value

## Agent workflow

- Restate the goal and the files you will touch before editing
- Work on a branch, not `main`. Understand → plan → prompt → review → refine. Do not accept output you cannot explain.
- First PR is done only if it is scoped, isolated, described, reviewable, self-verified, and aligned. Verify docs-only work by re-reading the diff.
- When unsure, consult `docs/onboarding/` and update the repo-map if the tree disagrees
- There is no `.github/` folder in this tree. If CI checks appear later, treat failures as blockers (orientation notes).
- Before Start/Router/Devtools edits, follow the Intent skill-loading block at the top of `AGENTS.md` (repo-map lists that file for Intent skill loading)

## Out of scope defaults

- No rewriting the app “for best practices” unprompted; no silent product-requirement changes
- No large refactors, dependency upgrades, schema changes, secrets, or unrelated “while I was here” edits
- Do not expand into `src/` unless a mentor or the task explicitly expands beyond Safe first-touch
